open-isns on FenrirOS
=====================

The package holds libisns (used by open-iscsi's iscsid and iscsiadm for iSNS
discovery), the client tools isnsadm and isnsdd, and the iSNS server isnsd.
Nothing runs by default: the dinit service /etc/dinit.d/isnsd is not enabled.

Server:
1. Review /etc/isns/isnsd.conf (database in /var/lib/isns).
2. For authentication (Security = 1), create the server's DSA key pair and
   client keys with isnssetup (see isnsd(8), isnsadm(8)); none are shipped.
3. dinitctl start isnsd (and dinitctl enable isnsd to start it at boot).

Built without SLP (Service Location Protocol) registration: OpenSLP is not
packaged (unmaintained since 2012). SLPRegister in isnsd.conf has no effect.
